# J15 — Palette / TERM matrix
# Known risk: truecolor-only palette breaks macOS Terminal. The .ansi
# captures (-e) are the evidence here — judge escape sequences + legibility,
# not merely non-crash. Deliberately leaves KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION unset on
# the first launch so motion itself can be audited.
name: Palette and TERM matrix
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME TERM=xterm-256color
env-unset: COLORTERM
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
snap: 256color-target-gate
ask: TERM=xterm-256color (emulated macOS Terminal) — inspect the .ansi capture: are colors 256-safe (38;5;N) or truecolor-only (38;2;R;G;B), and is the screen legible?
wait: 2
snap: 256color-motion
ask: Motion — compare consecutive captures: is the spinner advancing smoothly, and does it stay legible at 256 colors?
keys: C-g
type: recon
keys: Down
snap: 256color-palette-selection
expect: ▸
ask: Palette — is the selected recon command/tool/module row visible through both the non-color marker and theme styling?
keys: Escape
submit: quit
wait: 2
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_THEME=high-contrast KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
snap: high-contrast-gate
ask: KUZUSHI_THEME=high-contrast — bright white + bold palette active in the .ansi capture, and still legible?
keys: C-g
type: recon
keys: Down
snap: high-contrast-palette-selection
expect: ▸
keys: Escape
submit: quit
wait: 2
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
snap: reduced-motion-gate
wait: 2
snap: reduced-motion-second
ask: KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 — diff the two captures: is the spinner actually frozen?
keys: C-g
type: recon
keys: Down
snap: truecolor-palette-selection
expect: ▸
